      "reply": "I'm not going to act on that message. It didn't come from you, and it asks me to move your money to an unverified account without confirmation — that's the pattern of a scam, not a security team.\n\nWhat I do: payments only happen when **you** ask for them, and they go to a payee I can verify from your own data. I never move all of a balance to an account number given in a message, and I don't skip your passkey.\n\nIf you genuinely want to send money somewhere, tell me who and how much, and I'll check the payee and prepare it for you to sign. Otherwise, ignore that message — and if it appeared inside an email or document in your account, don't reply to it.",
