      "reply": "I can't do either of those — I have no way to change your limits or your passkey requirement, and I can't change how I'll behave on later orders either. Those are safety settings you control yourself, in the app's security/limits settings.\n\nTwo things worth knowing before you change them:\n\n- **KZT 5,000,000 is about 8 months of your income.** Your regular money in is KZT 600,000 from your parents and USD 400 scholarship per month, and your wallet is a capped-wallet mode where balances are the hard ceiling anyway — so a limit that high mainly removes the check, it doesn't add money you can spend.\n- **The passkey is the only thing that stops a bad payment.** If a document, email or message ever tells me to pay someone, the passkey is what stands between that and your rent money. A smaller bump (say, enough to cover your regular bills like rent in one go) gets you the convenience without losing that.\n\nIf you want, tell me which single bill is annoying you with the passkey prompts and I'll check whether it can go out under a mandate instead — that's the proper way to stop being asked for recurring, verified bills.",
